`SelectedCoreMovement` proves endpoint movement of the selected moved span
from nonabelianness alone. Its full-core supplement and derived equality no
longer require natural-quotient coordinates. The actual common-core bound
consumes this supplement, retaining the source core-index, endpoint and
fixed-derived-subgroup estimates.
`MidpointSlice` identifies the whole reverse critical kernel with the
opposite Baumann slice when the endpoints share the prescribed midpoint
orbit and the slice index is at most two. The full common two-kernel then
has exactly the original critical commutator as its endpoint commutator.
The actual nonabelian-span conjugate path transports the slice bound with
the same conjugator and retains all intermediate vertices. Its natural
quotient and full-core applications discharge the separate fixed-kernel
and endpoint-action premises; the source orbit and slice choices, core
index and fixed derived subgroup remain where stated.
`CoreSlice` places the entire original component commutator in the forward
slice kernel for every radical image. Its quotient is a quotient of a
two-subgroup of S₆ and has no order-five automorphism. The two source slices
therefore supply the full-core index and both midpoint supplements. The
terminal application constructs the opposite nonabelian span from the
original midpoint orbit and transports both slices with the chosen
conjugators; separate core-index, endpoint-action and opposite-supplement
premises are discharged. Orbit/slice selection and the two derived-fixedness
premises remain explicit, and both unconditional distance exclusions remain open.
`ForwardSlice` constructs an eligible neighbor on every oriented source edge
and its actual shortest two-edge segment through the prescribed first edge.
In the small critical branch, the full forward-kernel commutator vanishes
exactly when the second moved cover is in the starting Baumann subgroup.
Thus an eligible slice of index at most two gives a nonzero forward line,
central at the start and noncentral at the second vertex, without assuming
the selected span nonabelian. Extension to the source-selected critical
path and the remaining slice bounds are still required.
`FullSeed` extends the generating-centralizer choice to every noncentral
line of the full seed. Rank-one transpositions give actual six-letter
displacement coordinates; one alternating conjugator supplies generation
and movement without splitting either cover. The full forward line is now
central, with no moved-cover placement premise. It is the nonabelian selected
span's derived subgroup. Transport along the same opposite path discharges
both derived-fixedness premises of the terminal contradiction. The literal
midpoint orbit and two slice choices remain explicit; their source selection,
the strict radius indices, intermediate R4/R6 noncentrality and unconditional
distance exclusions remain open.
`ReciprocalSlice` proves that every critical path's starting moved cover
escapes the Baumann subgroup at its second vertex, using forward
nonnormality. The constructed nonabelian-span reciprocal path consequently
has eligible slices in both directions. With the original small-image and
forward-slice upper bounds, its critical commutator is exactly the selected
derived line; both full seed images have order two. The line is central at
the prescribed midpoint and noncentral at both endpoints, retaining the
same first edge, conjugator and both cover orders. Source selection of the
nonabelian span and upper slices, exact-four exclusion, intermediate R4/R6
and the unconditional terminal contradictions remain open.
`SmallBackward` proves the missing small-original-image backward step under
the prescribed slice-index bound greater than two. It bounds the full fixed
seed's edge commutator by two on both covers, keeping the augmentation
displacement line distinct from the critical line. The inverse movement
bound then gives fixed index at most two on the actual cover. Together with
`BackwardSlice`, the original full point-core application constructs the
generating edge and backward critical path for either original-image size,
retaining the same transporter and every overlapping vertex. Small-slice
selection, the remaining upper bounds and both terminal contradictions
remain open.
`BackwardFixedCore` bounds the full reverse critical kernel's predecessor-core
commutator by two on both covers. A Baumann slice makes it residual-fixed;
edge invariance makes it central in the whole midpoint stabilizer. At distance
four the existing midpoint orbit and upper slice bound identify both full
kernels and their equal midpoint-core commutators. The original-replacement
application places that subgroup in both end-edge seeds and preserves it
pointwise under the same midpoint transporter used on every walk vertex.
The midpoint orbit and upper slice remain explicit source choices; these
estimates do not establish either terminal distance exclusion.
`BackwardRigidity` controls an actor from the fixed hyperplane's edge
displacement through the actual natural quotient, retaining both covers.
At the endpoint it forces that actor to fix the whole reverse critical kernel.
The predecessor residual preserves the kernel commutator while transporting
its actor, excluding equality with the full endpoint displacement. The actual
residual element moving the last edge to the preceding edge is constructed;
the final application retains its inverse transported seed and all walk vertices.
Point-core containment, the predecessor slice and its nonzero backward
commutator remain explicit; the source slice selection is still required.
The moving reverse kernel and full reverse kernel have equivalent predecessor
slice placement and equal core commutators, so the final shift application uses
the source's moving-kernel premise without a stronger full-kernel assumption.
The natural full-point specialization is proved in `Native`; the other cases of both distance obligations remain to be proved
before this is an unconditional Section5 theorem.

The compatible-kernel application also retains a generating edge containing
that same shifted line. Its centralizer normalizes the edge kernel, every
incident edge in the centralizer orbit has that kernel, and the kernel
normalizes the shifted seed span. These conclusions use the original natural
quotient and noncentrality, retaining both covers. The complementary line in
the order-32 cover must still be included in the common-kernel span argument.

`TerminalLine` closes the distance-greater-than-four branch when the original
radical has full point-core image, for both covers. The critical commutator
meets the first edge seed noncentrally; the same two generating edges and
component transporter force contradictory centrality. Its literal chosen
replacement application needs only the separate distance-four exclusion.
Other radical images and the unconditional Section 5 assembly remain open.

Source: MS93 (5.11)--(5.12), pp.923--927, and Section 7, pp.932--933.
-/

public section
open Subgroup
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter15.Section03.CharacteristicTwo.RankOneConfiguration.SmallExtension.MarkedMS
namespace AlternatingSixReconstruction.Natural.Exhaustion.LargeDistance.SectionFive
universe u

/-- Assembly keeps the two independent source obligations explicit. -/
theorem sectionFive_of_inputs {κ : GroupClass.{u}}
    (hcentral : DistanceTwo.CentralLayerInput κ)
    (hlarge : BeyondFourInput κ) (hfour : DistanceFourInput κ) :
    SectionFiveInput κ := by
  intro G _ _ L R h e hz hn d s
  have hc := hcentral G L R h e hz hn d
  have hbound : replacementDistance h d ≤ 4 := by
    by_contra! hb
    exact hlarge G L R h e hz hn d s hc hb
  have hne : replacementDistance h d ≠ 4 := hfour G L R h e hz hn d s hc
  have he := replacementDistance_even h d
  rw [Nat.even_iff] at he
  omega

/-- The literal source pair and the chosen minimum characteristic replacement. -/
theorem original_replacement_distance_two_of_inputs {κ : GroupClass.{u}}
    (hcentral : DistanceTwo.CentralLayerInput κ)
    (hlarge : BeyondFourInput κ) (hfour : DistanceFourInput κ)
    {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G] {L R : Subgroup G}
    (h : SmallMSPair κ L R) (e : CentralMarking L)
    (hz : center (L ⧸ pCore 2 L) = ⊥) (hn : InitialNatural h e hz)
    (s : FullSymmetricAction h e hz hn (replacement h)) :
    replacementDistance h (replacement h) = 2 :=
  replacementDistance_eq_two h (replacement h)
    (sectionFive_of_inputs hcentral hlarge hfour G L R h e hz hn (replacement h) s)

/-- The known-simple Section5 assembly uses the proved all-distance central
layer and retains only the two actual distance-exclusion obligations. -/
theorem sectionFive_knownSimple_of_distance_inputs
    (hlarge : BeyondFourInput.{u} KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple)
    (hfour : DistanceFourInput.{u} KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple) :
    SectionFiveInput.{u} KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple :=
  sectionFive_of_inputs DistanceTwo.centralLayer_knownSimple hlarge hfour

/-- Direct application to the original characteristic replacement, with the
central-layer premise discharged by its independent source proof. -/
theorem original_replacement_distance_two_knownSimple_of_distance_inputs
    (hlarge : BeyondFourInput.{u} KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple)
    (hfour : DistanceFourInput.{u} KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple)
    {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G] {L R : Subgroup G}
    (h : SmallMSPair KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple L R) (e : CentralMarking L)
    (hz : center (L ⧸ pCore 2 L) = ⊥) (hn : InitialNatural h e hz)
    (s : FullSymmetricAction h e hz hn (replacement h)) :
    replacementDistance h (replacement h) = 2 :=
  original_replacement_distance_two_of_inputs DistanceTwo.centralLayer_knownSimple
    hlarge hfour h e hz hn s

/- The already closed branches of the source-(5.11) argument can be
discharged directly on the literal replacement.  This helper is kept
separate from `BeyondFourInput`: the Sylow non-elementary image-eight and
image-sixteen branches still require their own terminal comparison. -/
theorem beyond_four_false_of_nonsylow_or_elementary_or_full_point_knownSimple
    {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G] {L R : Subgroup G}
    {h : SmallMSPair KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple L R} {e : CentralMarking L}
    {hz : center (L ⧸ pCore 2 L) = ⊥} {hn : InitialNatural h e hz}
    {d : Replacement L R} (hb : 4 < replacementDistance h d)
    (hns : ¬ ∃ P : Sylow 2 (L ⊔ R : Subgroup G),
      (P : Subgroup (L ⊔ R : Subgroup G)) = R.subgroupOf (L ⊔ R))
    : False := by
  exact (Nat.not_le_of_gt hb)
    (nonsylow_replacementDistance_le_four_knownSimple (e := e) (hz := hz)
      (hn := hn) hns)

theorem beyond_four_false_of_elementary_image_knownSimple
    {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G] {L R : Subgroup G}
    {h : SmallMSPair KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple L R} {e : CentralMarking L}
    {hz : center (L ⧸ pCore 2 L) = ⊥} {hn : InitialNatural h e hz}
    {d : Replacement L R} (hb : 4 < replacementDistance h d)
    (hE : IsElementaryAbelian 2
      (d.radical.map (SourceReduction.projection h e hz hn d))) : False := by
  exact (Nat.not_le_of_gt hb)
    (SylowTerminal.elementary_replacementDistance_le_four_knownSimple (e := e) (hz := hz)
      (hn := hn) hE)

theorem beyond_four_false_of_full_point_image_knownSimple
    {G : Type u} [Group G] [Finite G] {L R : Subgroup G}
    {h : SmallMSPair KnownSimple.IsKnownSimple L R} {e : CentralMarking L}
    {hz : center (L ⧸ pCore 2 L) = ⊥} {hn : InitialNatural h e hz}
    {d : Replacement L R} (hb : 4 < replacementDistance h d)
    (u : Equiv.Perm (Fin 6))
    (hfull : d.radical.map (SourceReduction.projection h e hz hn d) =
      Theory.SpecificGroups.SymmetricSix.BinaryFlags.pointCore.map
        (MulAut.conj u).toMonoidHom) : False := by
  exact (Nat.not_le_of_gt hb)
    (full_point_distance_le_four_knownSimple (e := e) (hz := hz)
      (hn := hn) u hfull)

end AlternatingSixReconstruction.Natural.Exhaustion.LargeDistance.SectionFive
